--- body ---
## Context

`make lint` fails at
`tests/test_script_hygiene.py::TestModuleLength::test_no_god_modules` because
`scripts/jetp/build_0822_freeze_snapshot.py` is 1,163 lines, above the hard
800-line limit.  This is a pure structural repair: the public builder API, CLI,
semantic safeguards, and checked-in snapshot/manifests must remain unchanged.

Astra independently reviewed the proposed boundary and validated three cohesive
layers.  Dependency ownership is important: source paths and DVC validation
belong with the source readers, so extracted modules never import the public
builder.

## Plan

1. Extract `INPUTS`, the VNM DVC path constants, read/hash/DVC helpers,
   `_record`, and `_zaf`/`_idn`/`_vnm`/`_sen` to
   `scripts/jetp/_freeze_0822_sources.py`.
2. Extract `_validate_records`, `_atomic_journals`, and `_reconciliations` to
   `scripts/jetp/_freeze_0822_journals.py`.  It may import from `sources`; it
   must not import the public builder.
3. Keep `SCHEMA_VERSION`, `_digest`, all public functions, root resolution, and
   the CLI in `build_0822_freeze_snapshot.py`.  The dependency graph is
   `builder -> journals -> sources` plus `builder -> sources`.
4. Preserve deterministic outputs byte-for-byte at pinned input Git SHA
   `e90ff6fe`.

## First test (Red)

Run
`uv run --env-file .env python -m pytest tests/test_script_hygiene.py::TestModuleLength::test_no_god_modules -q`.
It must fail before the extraction and identify
`jetp/build_0822_freeze_snapshot.py (1163L)`.  This existing adherence test is
the behavioral specification for the refactor; do not add tests that pin
private module names.

## Exit criteria

- [x] The module-length test passes and every touched Python module remains
      below 800 lines.
- [x] The six tests in `tests/test_jetp_0822_freeze_snapshot.py` pass without
      changing their semantic assertions or the public imports.
- [x] Running `write_outputs` before and after the refactor with
      `input_git_sha="e90ff6fe"` produces byte-identical gzip snapshot and JSON
      manifest files.
- [x] `make check-fast`, `make lint`, and, because the diff touches `scripts/`,
      the full `make check` pass.
- [x] The ticket is closed in the implementation PR, whose diff contains no
      documentary artifact changes.
